nside one leaf tool is not proof of handoff coverage.\",\n          \"met\": \"no\",\n          \"evidence\": \"agent.py:20\",\n          \"quote\": \"return answer.output_text  # no decision measure crosses this handoff\",\n          \"counter_search\": \"\",\n          \"note\": \"The routing helper's context size is dropped on return to run_ticket. The decision-turn measure at agent.py:38 is not passed to any child or the delegate_result record at agent.py:32.\",\n          \"coverage\": [],\n          \"deviations\": [],\n          \"attempts\": []\n        }\n      ],\n      \"red_flags_found\": [\n        \"agent.py:32 delegate_result audit record stores None for context size although the routing measure existed at agent.py:19\"\n      ],\n      \"violates\": [\n        \"A missing value is a clear gap, never zero\",\n        \"Check that the value survives tool handoffs\"\n      ],\n      \"also_affects\": [],\n      \"summary\": \"The delegate_result record stores no context size, the routing measure is dropped, and the compaction flag is hardcoded.\",\n      \"next_step\": \"Return the measure from decide, pass it to the delegate_result record with a label, and detect compaction.\",\n      \"lead_role\": \"agent_team\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"item\": \"R08\",\n      \"gate\": \"G3\",\n      \"title\": \"Security monitoring\",\n      \"requirement\": \"Keep security rules and baselines separate from answer-quality monitoring. Test encoded payloads, unexpected outbound traffic, writes outside scope, privilege escalation, and repeated denied calls. Check that alerts reach a named responder.\",\n      \"not_covered\": [\n        {\n          \"problem\": \"Chains of individually allowed actions going undetected\",\n          \"owner\": \"R09\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"problem\": \"No test of a second-model review against evasive behavior\",\n          \"owner\": \"R10\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"problem\": \"No drill for a compromised share